WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.668
 Josh, Mareko, congratulations.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.304
Both of you made signature
blades that have propelled you

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:07.206
into the third round
of competition,

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.009
giving you a chance at the
title of Forged in Fire champion

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.245
and another shot
at that $10,000.

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:14.380
Well now, we're going to send
you back to your home forges

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:17.082
to recreate an iconic
blade from history.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:22.321
And that weapon is the Ida.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.457
 Awesome.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.292
WIL WILLIS: The Ida
is a long cutting

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:29.261
sword most commonly used by the
Yoruba people of West Africa.

00:00:29.361 --> 00:00:32.398
Their idolization of Ogun,
the god of metal and war,

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:34.700
led their blacksmiths
to be among the most

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.269
skilled in West Africa.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.672
With its leaf-shaped blade, that
can be single or double edged,

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:43.643
the Ida was a practical tool for
both agriculture and hunting,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.245
as well as a deadly
weapon on the battlefield.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.381
In combat, it was often
laced with pepper or poison

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:52.652
to paralyze enemies and ensured
that the slash of the Ida

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.154
left many dead in its wake.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:59.425
The length of the blade must
be between 22 and 26 inches.

00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:01.961
Additionally, it must
have a double edge.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.596
 I've never heard of
this weapon before.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.465
I mean, I've seen
weapons that are similar,

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.934
but I'm not really
a weapons expert.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.235
So if I come away
with a win, it's

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.403
not going to be a cheap win.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.972
I might make a great
blade and beat--

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.374
you know.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.508
I did last time.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.009
 You will have five
days at your home

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.377
forge to complete
this challenge.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.879
At the end of those
five days, you'll

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.615
return to present your finished
Idas to the panel of judges.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.250
 I'm really proud that
I've been able to make

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.818
it to the final round again.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.153
I feel like I have what it
takes to win this competition,

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.457
and I also really
want to win for Doug.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.627
WIL WILLIS: It's down to
just Doug and Jason's picks.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.162
Don't let them down.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.830
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.798
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:40.800
JOSH SMITH: Good luck.

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:41.868
MAREKO MAUMASI: Let's do this.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.671 line:14%
JOSH SMITH: Today's day one.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.873
I'm back home.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.874
It's a couple below
zero this morning.

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:50.276
It's time to get to work.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.878
I'm just going to stack up
a bill out of Damascus here.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.446
This is going to
be my river going

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:57.350
down the center of the blade,
alternating layers of steel.

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:58.918
I'm going to be doing
a really complicated

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.220
Damascus blade
with a lot of welds

00:02:01.286 --> 00:02:04.924
and a lot of chances for error.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.393
I was on the show
last season, and I

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.928
was absolutely happy and
proud of the Kora sword

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:10.796
when I built it.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:11.797
And I still am.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.199
Just didn't win.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.268
This is a bit of a shot
at redemption for me.

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:17.904
That thing's ready to twist.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.739
I'm twisting this metal to
give it a really cool pattern

00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:22.174
along the edge of this sword.

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:24.510
The twisting is a
very intense process,

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.646
and you're just really
watching that steel close,

00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:28.947
making sure you're not
shearing it in half.

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:29.982
I'm going to call that good.

00:02:30.048 --> 00:02:31.251
I don't want to push my luck.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.189
MAREKO MAUMASI: Back
at my home forge.

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:39.092
The challenge is to
build an Ida sword.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.027
My plan is to make kind of
a mosaic steel, which is

00:02:42.127 --> 00:02:43.663
aesthetically really beautiful.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:47.800
And into the forge and
the great white yonder.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.937
I'm going to do a full integral
blade, which means the blade,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.305
the guard, and the
full tang in the handle

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:56.542
are all going to be forged out
of the same piece of steel.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.577
Biggest concern is that
the welds might not take.

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:02.047
So I'm just going to keep my
fingers crossed, keep my cool,

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:04.150
and just do things
the way I normally do.

00:03:04.216 --> 00:03:06.953
And should come out just fine.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.256
Like I'm forging in
fire or something.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.324
See what I did there?

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:14.961
JOSH SMITH: It's day three.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.161
My blade's grown.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.830
I'm ready to heat treat.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.298
I'm feeling pretty anxious.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.500
Two days of work
comes down to this.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.369
You just never know what's
going to happen when

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:25.705
you actually go into that oil.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:26.606
Here goes nothing.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:35.882
OK.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.421
Baby looks as
straight as an arrow.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:46.592
This test piece that I
heat-treated with my sword,

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.361
I'm going to beat up a
little antler with it

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.562
and see how it does.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:54.333
That one took a chunk out there.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:56.602
I ended up with two chunks
in the end that were missing,

00:03:56.702 --> 00:03:59.739
but I don't feel like I have
time to play with right now.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.007
But I think I'll be fine.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:04.877
MAREKO MAUMASI: It's
pretty damn cold in here,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:09.349
so I use my little hobo
fire, an old turkey fryer.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:13.619
What's most important is getting
good heat treat on the blade.

00:04:13.685 --> 00:04:16.989
So I just need to bring it up
all to an even temperature,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.658
pull it out, and
give her a quench.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:29.001
All right, that
should be plenty.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:31.103
Still looks pretty
dang straight.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.504
Woo-hoo!

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:35.107
I actually feel a little
bit ahead of where I thought

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.275
I was going to be today.

00:04:36.341 --> 00:04:38.711
My integral guard
area is in there.

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.046
I got my full tang.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:43.549
So the rest of it pretty much
from this point on is grinding.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.021 line:8%
JOSH SMITH: It's time
to start a handle.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:51.524
The handle's what cost me
the competition last year.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.393
I'm going to choose
this African Blackwood.

00:04:54.459 --> 00:04:56.295
This sword is from West Africa.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:59.932
So I'm trying to keep
it somewhat authentic.

00:05:00.032 --> 00:05:04.270
I fight this battle between
staying historically correct

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:07.807
and making something that
the judges can hang on to.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:09.175
It's looking good.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.010
I want the look to
be a bit of my own.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:14.981
Sword blade is real Ida,
and the handle is real Josh.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.486
What the-- [bleep]?

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.921
There's a hole in the wood.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.161
What the-- [bleep]?

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:32.365
The frickin'-- there's
a hole in the wood.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.866
Right in the middle
of the block.

00:05:33.932 --> 00:05:36.769 line:8%
Usually when you see a little
pinhole like that pop up

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.238 line:8%
and you keep grinding, it
just gets bigger and bigger,

00:05:39.304 --> 00:05:40.973
and you've ruined the handle.

00:05:41.039 --> 00:05:43.776
I actually think I might be
able to file through it tomorrow

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:44.944
if I have time.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.179
Today was a pretty wearing
day, but in the end,

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.248
I've got a sword
with a handle on it.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:52.551 line:8%
I'm pretty comfortable
with where I'm at.

00:05:52.651 --> 00:05:54.153 line:8%
MAREKO MAUMASI: We're
in the home stretch.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.955 line:8%
I just have some
light finish work

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:59.459 line:8%
to touch back up on the
blade before I etch it,

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:03.996
and then reattach the handle,
and then sharpen the thing.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:06.833
Feels like it's got a
little bit of a tippy edge.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.104
It'll definitely cut.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.706
I feel really good about what
I was able to accomplish.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:17.242
Question is whether or not
it's actually going to survive.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:19.278
There's only one
way to find out.

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:22.448
And that's to let
Doug play with it.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.150
DOUG MARCAIDA: This
is a kill test.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.520
To see how lethal your weapons
are, I will take your weapons

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.889
and deliver multiple
slashes and hacks

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:32.090
on these ballistic dummies.

00:06:32.157 --> 00:06:32.892
Josh, you're up first.

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:33.826
Are you ready?

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:34.627
JOSH SMITH: I'm ready.

00:06:34.693 --> 00:06:35.494
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.396
JOSH SMITH: All right.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.431
Those ballistics dummies
are pretty tough.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.267
They're a hard
thing to lacerate.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:44.970
So this test makes me
a little bit nervous.

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:48.541
[electric guitar music]

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:03.823
DOUG MARCAIDA: OK, Josh.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.658
This is a wicked blade.

00:07:05.724 --> 00:07:07.793
On the initial hack
right here, the blade

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:11.229
went all the way through into
the ribs and broke those ribs.

00:07:11.296 --> 00:07:12.664
The other side, same thing.

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:15.167
That would disembowel
this dummy.

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:16.969
Your weapon will kill.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:18.404
JOSH SMITH: Thank you.
DOUG MARCAIDA: Good job.

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:19.671
JOSH SMITH: Thank you very much.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:20.873
DOUG MARCAIDA:
Mareko, you're next.

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:22.141
You ready?
MAREKO MAUMASI: I'm ready.

00:07:22.207 --> 00:07:23.042
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.677
MAREKO MAUMASI: All right.

00:07:24.743 --> 00:07:26.846
I don't know how well
my weapon's actually

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.748
going to perform because it
has kind of a beefier edge

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:32.018
geometry, which
doesn't necessarily

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:35.454
lend it to slicing very well.

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:38.724
[electric guitar music]

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:54.673
DOUG MARCAIDA: Well,
Mareko, it is sharp.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.244
As you can see what it did, it
lacerated right in all the way

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.647
to the chest cavity, breaking
the ribs that are in there.

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:03.983
On the horizontal
slashes, same thing.

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:05.551
It lacerated deep.

00:08:05.617 --> 00:08:11.424
Feels good, balances out,
and your blade will kill.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.358
Good job.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.726
MAREKO MAUMASI: Thank you.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.961
DOUG MARCAIDA: Next up
is the sharpness test.

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.598
To test your double edged
sword, I will take your weapon

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:22.534
and deliver three slashes per
blade across this web of ropes.

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:26.639
If your Ida is sharp, it
should meet no resistance.

00:08:26.739 --> 00:08:27.773
Josh, you're up first.

00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:28.440
Are you ready?

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:29.508
JOSH SMITH: Let's do it.

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:32.210
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:08:32.277 --> 00:08:35.915
[electric guitar music]

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:48.827
I'll tell you, Josh,
this is definitely sharp.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.764
It met no resistance
cutting through the ropes.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:53.565
It feels good in the hand.

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:56.469
Your sword, sir, will cut.

00:08:56.569 --> 00:08:57.503
Good job.

00:08:57.569 --> 00:08:58.336
JOSH SMITH: Thank you very much.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.671
Appreciate it.

00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:00.672
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Mareko, you ready?

00:09:00.772 --> 00:09:01.707
MAREKO MAUMASI: Bring it on.

00:09:01.773 --> 00:09:04.276
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:07.547
[electric guitar music]

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.992
Well, Mareko, your
blade is fast.

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.093
It's light.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.195
It did lacerate through
some of the ropes,

00:09:23.295 --> 00:09:24.997
and some of them it didn't.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:28.467
Overall though,
your blade will cut.

00:09:28.533 --> 00:09:29.802
MAREKO MAUMASI: Thanks, Doug.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.704
DOUG MARCAIDA: Next up
is the strength test.

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:33.806
Dave?

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:35.907
DAVID BAKER: Gentlemen, to test
the strength and durability

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:38.376
of your blades, I'm going to
chop into these femur bones

00:09:38.443 --> 00:09:39.611
three times.

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:41.313
Now, the point of
this test is not

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.948
to see how many
bones I can break,

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.117
but to see how well
your blades hold

00:09:45.184 --> 00:09:47.319
up through that punishment.

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:48.454
Josh, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:49.421
JOSH SMITH: I'm ready.

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:50.389
DAVID BAKER: All right.

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:53.693
[electric guitar music]

00:10:09.574 --> 00:10:10.376
JOSH SMITH: Damn.

00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:19.284
DAVID BAKER: Everything
stayed straight.

00:10:19.384 --> 00:10:20.853
Everything stayed tight.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:25.691
But you can see we've got some
extreme chipping on that blade.

00:10:25.758 --> 00:10:28.394
Did sizable damage to
what we were swinging at,

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:33.866
but you can just
see those chips.

00:10:33.932 --> 00:10:36.468
All right, Mareko, you ready?

00:10:36.534 --> 00:10:39.071
MAREKO MAUMASI: [laughs] Yeah.

00:10:39.138 --> 00:10:40.439
DAVID BAKER: All right.

00:10:40.506 --> 00:10:43.275 line:8%
MAREKO MAUMASI: I did my best
to make the geometry so it could

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:44.710 line:14%
withstand this kind of use.

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:47.613
But seeing the damage that
happened to Josh's sword

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:51.050
makes my heart, like,
sink down in my stomach.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.153
[electric guitar music]

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:16.442
DAVID BAKER: Well, Mareko, you
did pick up that slight bend,

00:11:16.508 --> 00:11:18.276
but your edges are beautiful.

00:11:18.376 --> 00:11:21.246
They've held up quite nicely.

00:11:21.346 --> 00:11:22.147
Nicely done.

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:23.683
MAREKO MAUMASI: Thanks.

00:11:23.783 --> 00:11:26.085
WIL WILLIS: Josh, Mareko,
it was definitely a battle.

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:28.653
But there can only
be one champion.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:33.491
The Judges' Pick Forged in
Fire champion is Mareko.

00:11:33.592 --> 00:11:34.726
Congratulations.

00:11:34.826 --> 00:11:37.195
You are the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:38.163
Good job.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:38.964
MAREKO MAUMASI: Wow.

00:11:39.064 --> 00:11:39.832
JOSH SMITH: Congratulations.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:42.635
[interposing voices]

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:47.105
WIL WILLIS: Josh, please
surrender your weapon.

00:11:47.172 --> 00:11:49.574
JOSH SMITH: I feel they
made the right decision.

00:11:49.641 --> 00:11:51.310
I may not be the Forged
in Fire champion,

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.779
but I'm still a great
bladesmith and a better dad.

00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.582
But I showed my kids that you
step up and you do it again,

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:58.183
and you give it your best.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.752
And I think I did that, and
I brought a beautiful sword.

00:11:59.818 --> 00:12:04.957
Looks nice, but looks don't cut.

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:07.693
WIL WILLIS: Mareko, how does
it feel rising to the top,

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.595
earning a check for $10,000,
and being the Judges'

00:12:10.695 --> 00:12:11.897
Pick Forged in Fire champion?

00:12:11.997 --> 00:12:13.232
MAREKO MAUMASI:
Yeah, it's definitely

00:12:13.299 --> 00:12:14.867
been a serious challenge.

00:12:14.934 --> 00:12:18.504
But to be able to represent for
Doug, a man who I respect very

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:20.672
much, and to make it
to the end and win,

00:12:20.739 --> 00:12:22.208
that makes me really proud.

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:24.176
I came so close to
winning last time.

00:12:24.243 --> 00:12:27.179
It feels really good that
I was actually able to pull

00:12:27.246 --> 00:12:28.380
off the win this time.

00:12:28.481 --> 00:12:30.849
Winning the $10,000, it's
going to be so helpful

00:12:30.916 --> 00:12:32.651
for myself and my family.

00:12:32.717 --> 00:12:34.586
Doug, your horse won the race.

00:12:34.652 --> 00:12:36.622
I hope that I made you proud.

00:12:36.688 --> 00:12:39.191
So thanks for
bringing me back, man.

00:12:39.258 --> 00:12:42.294
[electric guitar music]

